{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1310729-question-for-current-2e-games","id":1310729,"title":"Question for current 2E games","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-05-08T05:40:14-07:00","id":1310729,"title":"Question for current 2E games","content":"I am spinning up a few games and have a question for those who are currently in games.<br /> <br /> How important/lengthy is 'Episode Zero'?<br /> <br /> From my point of view, Episode Zero is the night where the group first gets together to discuss the campaign and talk through characters. As there are usually limited physical copies of the rules, this benefits my group most times. Looking through the pdfs, I notice that it would be helpful to chargen were everyone together to discuss team roles.<br /> <br /> Is this the case in existing games?<br /> How long did chargen take?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1011-phgraves","name":"PHGraves","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1011_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-08T07:12:21-07:00","id":1310742,"title":"","content":"As I have stable gaming group I run currently other games ( finally! ) we made 'Months of Zero' - it's not a one session, it's whole weeks we get to prepare the game. I as ST simply make new private Facebook group and slowly, one topic at time each week / month, we talk about future chronicle. For now, we have chosen 3 main Pantheons in play ( Aesir, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1278397-2e-bogovi-slavic-pantheon\">Slavic Bogi</a> and Theoi ) and location of story - Kiev, Ukraine. With final PDFs of Origin and Hero, players are finally starting to make their characters. All of this unfolds now on 3rd month of slow talks. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-08T09:56:21-07:00","id":1310768,"title":"","content":"Session 0 is important for any game in any system. It's a chance to discuss general ideas and to catch issues that might kill the campaign if ignored. For example, if the players and GM have vastly different ideas of the sort games they want to run.<br /> <br /> If the GM wants to run something akin to Indiana Jones and the players want to do something more like Avengers, there will be conflicts that arise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3961-thrythlind","name":"Thrythlind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-08T10:50:50-07:00","id":1310775,"title":"","content":"I think Session 0 is the point where the characters are prepared and discussed. It\u2019s virtually impossible to play session 1 without session 0.<br /> <br /> But, discussing the possible campaign is not a session 0 business, it must be done before even session 0. I mean, I wha t to play Indiana Jones, it\u2019s not going to be when we are thinking about the characters that we are going to say, \u201coh men... We are going for Indian Jones, not Avenges... so, just throw the ideas you have away and create a new one.\u201d<br /> <br /> I played once a Space Cowboys session that turned into a starcraft campaign... the guys was thinking about some desert planet where the confederation of planets mine some rare minerals. They would face some criminals on a SciFi western style, maybe fly to another planet or space station, and suddenly it was Mars Sara. Zergs show up, and they leave the planet with Jim Raynor... it was awesome, but at first moment the zergs let many people angry with the previous investigation endup in the thrash...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-09T07:03:47-07:00","id":1310967,"title":"","content":"All good points, but my question was more towards the relative importance of having the players work together when making characters due to the Band-related path.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1011-phgraves","name":"PHGraves","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1011_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-09T07:35:56-07:00","id":1310975,"title":"","content":"It depends a lot. I personally like the idea of the players working together and completing each other, so there is a need of communication and decisions to be made as a group. But I learned to play with D&amp;D, so I might be Biased...<br /> <br /> It was quite usual when we played Vampire and Mage back in the day, to let each player to build their character and than kind of force them together by a higher power. It usually makes the session 0 exist as more like a How did the characters end up together and less about character design.<br /> <br /> I guess, the results of a group working together is a better and more complete team, while the other way is a more organic way of storytelling... the challenges can be higher if the group is designed, but usually there is no redundancy in the team, there is 1 healer, 1 tank, one damage dealer and 1 crowd control for combat, them out of combat there is 1 social expert, 1 technology expert, 1 pilot/transporter and maybe 1 survivalist. When each character is made alone, the result usually is a bunch of jack of all trades, maybe some specialisation here and there but they can do a bit of everything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-09T11:21:25-07:00","id":1311017,"title":"","content":"A session zero is also useful so that you can get information from your players. Chiefly: &quot;What kind of game do you want to play? What sorts of things are you looking for?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}